{"format":1,"manifest":{"name":"cheat-sheets","publisher":"vyloxi","version":"1.0.0","displayName":"Cheat Sheets","description":"Searchable reference panels for Git, regular expressions, Vim, Markdown, HTTP status codes, CSS Flexbox and CSS Grid.","engines":{"ferrum":"^0.1.0"},"categories":["Productivity"],"icon":"icon.png","repository":"https://github.com/voukengdongmofrankysteve/ferrum-market","license":"MIT","main":"extension.js","activationEvents":["onCommand:cheatSheets.pick","onCommand:cheatSheets.search","onCommand:cheatSheets.git","onCommand:cheatSheets.regex","onCommand:cheatSheets.vim","onCommand:cheatSheets.markdown","onCommand:cheatSheets.http","onCommand:cheatSheets.flexbox","onCommand:cheatSheets.grid"],"permissions":[],"contributes":{"commands":[{"command":"cheatSheets.pick","title":"Open a Cheat Sheet...","category":"Cheat Sheets"},{"command":"cheatSheets.search","title":"Search All Cheat Sheets...","category":"Cheat Sheets"},{"command":"cheatSheets.git","title":"Git Cheat Sheet","category":"Cheat Sheets"},{"command":"cheatSheets.regex","title":"Regular expressions Cheat Sheet","category":"Cheat Sheets"},{"command":"cheatSheets.vim","title":"Vim Cheat Sheet","category":"Cheat Sheets"},{"command":"cheatSheets.markdown","title":"Markdown Cheat Sheet","category":"Cheat Sheets"},{"command":"cheatSheets.http","title":"HTTP status codes Cheat Sheet","category":"Cheat Sheets"},{"command":"cheatSheets.flexbox","title":"CSS Flexbox Cheat Sheet","category":"Cheat Sheets"},{"command":"cheatSheets.grid","title":"CSS Grid Cheat Sheet","category":"Cheat Sheets"}],"keybindings":[{"command":"cheatSheets.search","key":"Ctrl+Alt+K"}]}},"files":{"icon.png":{"encoding":"base64","content":""},"extension.js":{"encoding":"utf8","content":"// Cheat Sheets: searchable reference panels for Git, regular expressions, Vim, Markdown, HTTP status codes, CSS Flexbox and CSS Grid.\n// Click a row to put its code into your file. No permissions.\n\nconst SHEETS = {\n  git: {\n    title: 'Git',\n    groups: {\n      'Start': [['git init', 'Create a repository in this folder'], ['git clone <url>', 'Copy a repository'], ['git clone --depth 1 <url>', 'Copy only the latest snapshot (fast)'], ['git config --global user.name \"Name\"', 'Set your name'], ['git config --global user.email \"me@example.com\"', 'Set your email']],\n      'Save work': [['git status', 'What changed'], ['git add <file>', 'Stage a file'], ['git add -p', 'Stage piece by piece'], ['git add .', 'Stage everything'], ['git commit -m \"message\"', 'Save the staged changes'], ['git commit --amend', 'Change the last commit'], ['git commit --amend --no-edit', 'Add staged files to the last commit'], ['git diff', 'Unstaged changes'], ['git diff --staged', 'Staged changes']],\n      'Branches': [['git branch', 'List branches'], ['git switch -c <name>', 'Create and switch to a branch'], ['git switch <name>', 'Switch branch'], ['git branch -d <name>', 'Delete a merged branch'], ['git branch -D <name>', 'Delete a branch for sure'], ['git branch -m <new>', 'Rename the current branch'], ['git merge <name>', 'Merge a branch into this one'], ['git merge --abort', 'Stop a merge in trouble'], ['git rebase <name>', 'Replay your commits on top of another branch'], ['git rebase -i HEAD~3', 'Edit the last 3 commits'], ['git cherry-pick <commit>', 'Copy one commit here']],\n      'Remotes': [['git remote -v', 'List remotes'], ['git remote add origin <url>', 'Add a remote'], ['git fetch', 'Download without merging'], ['git pull', 'Download and merge'], ['git pull --rebase', 'Download and replay your commits'], ['git push', 'Upload commits'], ['git push -u origin <branch>', 'Upload a new branch and remember it'], ['git push --force-with-lease', 'Safer force push'], ['git push origin --delete <branch>', 'Delete a remote branch']],\n      'History': [['git log --oneline --graph --decorate', 'Short history with branches'], ['git log -p <file>', 'History of a file with changes'], ['git log --author=\"name\"', 'Commits by a person'], ['git log -S\"text\"', 'Commits that added or removed text'], ['git show <commit>', 'One commit'], ['git blame <file>', 'Who wrote each line'], ['git shortlog -sn', 'Commits per person'], ['git reflog', 'Everything HEAD did (find lost commits)']],\n      'Undo': [['git restore <file>', 'Throw away changes in a file'], ['git restore --staged <file>', 'Unstage a file'], ['git reset --soft HEAD~1', 'Undo the last commit, keep changes staged'], ['git reset HEAD~1', 'Undo the last commit, keep changes'], ['git reset --hard HEAD~1', 'Undo the last commit and its changes'], ['git revert <commit>', 'Make a new commit that undoes one'], ['git clean -fd', 'Delete untracked files and folders'], ['git checkout -- .', 'Throw away all unstaged changes (old way)']],\n      'Stash': [['git stash', 'Put changes aside'], ['git stash -u', 'Also stash untracked files'], ['git stash list', 'List stashes'], ['git stash pop', 'Bring the last stash back'], ['git stash apply stash@{1}', 'Apply a stash and keep it'], ['git stash drop', 'Delete the last stash']],\n      'Tags': [['git tag', 'List tags'], ['git tag -a v1.0.0 -m \"Release 1.0.0\"', 'Make an annotated tag'], ['git push origin v1.0.0', 'Upload one tag'], ['git push --tags', 'Upload all tags'], ['git tag -d v1.0.0', 'Delete a local tag']],\n    },\n  },\n  regex: {\n    title: 'Regular expressions',\n    groups: {\n      'Characters': [['.', 'Any character except a newline'], ['\\\\d', 'A digit'], ['\\\\D', 'Not a digit'], ['\\\\w', 'Letter, digit or underscore'], ['\\\\W', 'Not a word character'], ['\\\\s', 'Whitespace'], ['\\\\S', 'Not whitespace'], ['[abc]', 'a, b or c'], ['[^abc]', 'Anything but a, b, c'], ['[a-z]', 'A range'], ['\\\\.', 'A real dot (escape special characters)'], ['\\\\p{L}', 'Any letter in any language (u flag)']],\n      'Anchors': [['^', 'Start of the line'], ['$', 'End of the line'], ['\\\\b', 'A word boundary'], ['\\\\B', 'Not a word boundary'], ['\\\\A', 'Start of the text (some engines)'], ['\\\\z', 'End of the text (some engines)']],\n      'Quantifiers': [['*', '0 or more'], ['+', '1 or more'], ['?', '0 or 1'], ['{3}', 'Exactly 3'], ['{3,}', '3 or more'], ['{3,5}', '3 to 5'], ['*?', '0 or more, as few as possible (lazy)'], ['+?', '1 or more, lazy']],\n      'Groups': [['(abc)', 'Capture group'], ['(?:abc)', 'Group without capturing'], ['(?<name>abc)', 'Named group'], ['\\\\1', 'The text of group 1 again'], ['a|b', 'a or b'], ['(?=abc)', 'Followed by abc (lookahead)'], ['(?!abc)', 'Not followed by abc'], ['(?<=abc)', 'Preceded by abc (lookbehind)'], ['(?<!abc)', 'Not preceded by abc']],\n      'Flags': [['i', 'Ignore case'], ['g', 'Find all matches'], ['m', '^ and $ match at each line'], ['s', 'Dot also matches newlines'], ['u', 'Unicode mode'], ['x', 'Allow spaces and comments (some engines)']],\n      'Replace': [['$1', 'Insert group 1 (JavaScript, Rust, sed -E uses \\\\1)'], ['$&', 'Insert the whole match (JavaScript)'], ['\\\\1', 'Insert group 1 (Python, sed, editors)'], ['$<name>', 'Insert a named group (JavaScript)']],\n      'Common': [['^[\\\\w.+-]+@[\\\\w-]+(?:\\\\.[\\\\w-]+)+$', 'Email address (simple)'], ['https?://[\\\\w.-]+(?:/[^\\\\s]*)?', 'Web address'], ['\\\\d{4}-\\\\d{2}-\\\\d{2}', 'Date as 2026-10-22'], ['^#(?:[0-9a-fA-F]{3}){1,2}$', 'Hex color'], ['^\\\\s+|\\\\s+$', 'Spaces at both ends'], ['\\\\b(\\\\w+)\\\\s+\\\\1\\\\b', 'A repeated word']],\n    },\n  },\n  vim: {\n    title: 'Vim',\n    groups: {\n      'Modes': [['i', 'Insert before the cursor'], ['a', 'Insert after the cursor'], ['o', 'New line below'], ['O', 'New line above'], ['v', 'Select characters'], ['V', 'Select lines'], ['Ctrl+v', 'Select a block'], ['Esc', 'Back to normal mode'], [':', 'Command line']],\n      'Move': [['h j k l', 'Left, down, up, right'], ['w / b', 'Next / previous word'], ['e', 'End of the word'], ['0 / ^ / $', 'Line start / first character / end'], ['gg / G', 'Top / bottom of the file'], ['{n}G', 'Go to line n'], ['{ / }', 'Previous / next paragraph'], ['%', 'Matching bracket'], ['Ctrl+u / Ctrl+d', 'Half page up / down'], ['f{c} / t{c}', 'To a character on the line / just before it'], ['* / #', 'Next / previous match of the word']],\n      'Edit': [['x', 'Delete a character'], ['dd', 'Delete the line'], ['dw', 'Delete a word'], ['D', 'Delete to the end of the line'], ['cw', 'Change a word'], ['cc', 'Change the line'], ['yy', 'Copy the line'], ['p / P', 'Paste after / before'], ['u', 'Undo'], ['Ctrl+r', 'Redo'], ['.', 'Repeat the last change'], ['>> / <<', 'Indent / outdent'], ['J', 'Join the next line'], ['~', 'Toggle case'], ['ciw', 'Change the word under the cursor'], ['di\"', 'Delete inside quotes']],\n      'Search': [['/text', 'Search forward'], ['?text', 'Search backward'], ['n / N', 'Next / previous match'], [':%s/old/new/g', 'Replace everywhere'], [':%s/old/new/gc', 'Replace, ask each time'], [':noh', 'Clear highlighting']],\n      'Files': [[':w', 'Save'], [':q', 'Quit'], [':wq', 'Save and quit'], [':q!', 'Quit without saving'], [':e file', 'Open a file'], [':sp / :vsp', 'Split horizontally / vertically'], ['Ctrl+w w', 'Switch window'], [':bn / :bp', 'Next / previous buffer']],\n      'Macros and marks': [['qa', 'Record a macro in register a'], ['q', 'Stop recording'], ['@a', 'Play macro a'], ['ma', 'Set mark a'], [\"'a\", 'Jump to mark a'], ['\"ayy', 'Copy a line into register a'], ['\"ap', 'Paste register a']],\n    },\n  },\n  markdown: {\n    title: 'Markdown',\n    groups: {\n      'Text': [['# Heading 1', 'Heading level 1 (use ## for 2, ### for 3)'], ['**bold**', 'Bold'], ['*italic*', 'Italic'], ['~~strike~~', 'Strikethrough'], ['`code`', 'Inline code'], ['> quote', 'Quote'], ['---', 'Horizontal line'], ['text  \\n', 'Line break (two spaces at the end)']],\n      'Lists': [['- item', 'Bullet list'], ['1. item', 'Numbered list'], ['- [ ] task', 'Task, not done'], ['- [x] task', 'Task, done'], ['  - nested', 'Nested item (indent by 2 spaces)']],\n      'Links and images': [['[text](https://example.com)', 'Link'], ['[text](https://example.com \"title\")', 'Link with a title'], ['![alt text](image.png)', 'Image'], ['<https://example.com>', 'Automatic link'], ['[text][ref]\\n\\n[ref]: https://example.com', 'Reference link'], ['[![alt](badge.svg)](https://example.com)', 'Image that is a link']],\n      'Code': [['```js\\ncode\\n```', 'Code block with a language'], ['    code', 'Code block by indenting 4 spaces']],\n      'Tables': [['| A | B |\\n| --- | --- |\\n| 1 | 2 |', 'Table'], ['| Left | Center | Right |\\n| :--- | :---: | ---: |', 'Column alignment']],\n      'Extras': [['[^1]\\n\\n[^1]: The note.', 'Footnote'], ['<details>\\n<summary>Title</summary>\\n\\nText\\n\\n</details>', 'Collapsible section'], ['<!-- comment -->', 'Comment'], ['\\\\*', 'Show a special character']],\n    },\n  },\n  http: {\n    title: 'HTTP status codes',\n    groups: {\n      '1xx Information': [['100', 'Continue'], ['101', 'Switching Protocols'], ['103', 'Early Hints']],\n      '2xx Success': [['200', 'OK'], ['201', 'Created'], ['202', 'Accepted (will be done later)'], ['204', 'No Content'], ['206', 'Partial Content (range request)']],\n      '3xx Redirection': [['301', 'Moved Permanently'], ['302', 'Found (temporary redirect)'], ['303', 'See Other (go GET another page after a POST)'], ['304', 'Not Modified (use your cache)'], ['307', 'Temporary Redirect, same method'], ['308', 'Permanent Redirect, same method']],\n      '4xx Client error': [['400', 'Bad Request'], ['401', 'Unauthorized (not signed in)'], ['403', 'Forbidden (signed in, not allowed)'], ['404', 'Not Found'], ['405', 'Method Not Allowed'], ['406', 'Not Acceptable'], ['408', 'Request Timeout'], ['409', 'Conflict'], ['410', 'Gone (removed for good)'], ['413', 'Payload Too Large'], ['415', 'Unsupported Media Type'], ['418', \"I'm a teapot\"], ['422', 'Unprocessable Content (validation failed)'], ['429', 'Too Many Requests (rate limit)'], ['451', 'Unavailable For Legal Reasons']],\n      '5xx Server error': [['500', 'Internal Server Error'], ['501', 'Not Implemented'], ['502', 'Bad Gateway'], ['503', 'Service Unavailable'], ['504', 'Gateway Timeout']],\n    },\n  },\n  flexbox: {\n    title: 'CSS Flexbox',\n    groups: {\n      'Container': [['display: flex;', 'Start a flex container'], ['display: inline-flex;', 'Flex container that sits inline'], ['flex-direction: row;', 'Left to right (also row-reverse, column, column-reverse)'], ['flex-wrap: wrap;', 'Let items go to the next line'], ['gap: 1rem;', 'Space between items'], ['justify-content: center;', 'Along the main axis (flex-start, flex-end, space-between, space-around, space-evenly)'], ['align-items: center;', 'Across the main axis (flex-start, flex-end, stretch, baseline)'], ['align-content: space-between;', 'Space between lines when wrapping']],\n      'Items': [['flex: 1;', 'Grow to share the free space'], ['flex: 0 0 200px;', 'Fixed width, never grows or shrinks'], ['flex-grow: 1;', 'How much it grows'], ['flex-shrink: 0;', 'Do not shrink'], ['flex-basis: 30%;', 'Starting size'], ['align-self: flex-end;', 'Override align-items for this item'], ['order: -1;', 'Move to the front'], ['margin-left: auto;', 'Push this item and the next ones to the right']],\n      'Recipes': [['display: flex;\\njustify-content: center;\\nalign-items: center;', 'Center something both ways'], ['display: flex;\\njustify-content: space-between;\\nalign-items: center;', 'A navigation bar'], ['display: flex;\\nflex-direction: column;\\nmin-height: 100vh;', 'Sticky footer layout: give main flex: 1'], ['display: flex;\\nflex-wrap: wrap;\\ngap: 1rem;', 'Cards that wrap']],\n    },\n  },\n  grid: {\n    title: 'CSS Grid',\n    groups: {\n      'Container': [['display: grid;', 'Start a grid'], ['grid-template-columns: 1fr 2fr;', 'Two columns, the second twice as wide'], ['grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);', 'Three equal columns'], ['grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(220px, 1fr));', 'As many columns as fit'], ['grid-template-rows: auto 1fr auto;', 'Header, content, footer'], ['gap: 1rem;', 'Space between cells'], ['grid-template-areas: \"header header\" \"side main\";', 'Name the areas'], ['justify-items: center;', 'Align items inside cells, horizontally'], ['align-items: center;', 'Align items inside cells, vertically'], ['place-items: center;', 'Both of the above'], ['justify-content: center;', 'Place the whole grid in its box'], ['grid-auto-flow: dense;', 'Fill holes']],\n      'Items': [['grid-column: 1 / 3;', 'From line 1 to line 3'], ['grid-column: span 2;', 'Cover two columns'], ['grid-row: 1 / -1;', 'From the first to the last row line'], ['grid-area: header;', 'Put it in a named area'], ['justify-self: end;', 'Align this item horizontally'], ['align-self: start;', 'Align this item vertically']],\n      'Recipes': [['display: grid;\\ngrid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(240px, 1fr));\\ngap: 1rem;', 'A responsive card grid'], ['display: grid;\\nplace-items: center;\\nmin-height: 100vh;', 'Center something in the page'], ['display: grid;\\ngrid-template-columns: 240px 1fr;\\ngrid-template-rows: auto 1fr auto;\\nmin-height: 100vh;', 'Sidebar layout with header and footer'], ['aspect-ratio: 16 / 9;', 'Keep a shape (works on grid items too)']],\n    },\n  },\n};\n\nconst esc = (s) => String(s).replace(/&/g, '&amp;').replace(/</g, '&lt;').replace(/>/g, '&gt;').replace(/\"/g, '&quot;');\n\n/** Every row of a sheet as { group, code, note }. */\nfunction rows(key) {\n  const sheet = SHEETS[key];\n  if (!sheet) return [];\n  return Object.entries(sheet.groups).flatMap(([group, list]) => list.map(([code, note]) => ({ group, code, note })));\n}\n\nfunction filter(key, q) {\n  const s = String(q || '').trim().toLowerCase();\n  return rows(key).filter((r) => !s || r.code.toLowerCase().includes(s) || r.note.toLowerCase().includes(s) || r.group.toLowerCase().includes(s));\n}\n\nfunction page(key) {\n  const sheet = SHEETS[key];\n  const body = Object.entries(sheet.groups)\n    .map(([g, list]) => `<h4>${esc(g)}</h4>${list.map(([code, note]) => `<div class=\"r\" data-c=\"${esc(code)}\" data-q=\"${esc((g + ' ' + code + ' ' + note).toLowerCase())}\"><code>${esc(code).replace(/\\n/g, '<br>')}</code><span>${esc(note)}</span></div>`).join('')}`)\n    .join('');\n  return `<style>\n  body { font-family: var(--ui); } h3 { margin: 0 0 8px; } h4 { margin: 18px 0 6px; color: var(--accent); font-size: 12px; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: .05em; }\n  input { width: 100%; box-sizing: border-box; background: var(--raised, transparent); color: var(--fg); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 6px; padding: 8px 10px; font: 14px var(--ui); outline: none; } input:focus { border-color: var(--accent); }\n  .r { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(150px, 1fr) 1.3fr; gap: 14px; padding: 5px 8px; border-radius: 5px; cursor: pointer; align-items: baseline; } .r:hover { background: var(--raised, rgba(128,128,128,.15)); }\n  code { font: 12.5px/1.5 var(--mono, monospace); word-break: break-all; } .r span { color: var(--fg-dim); font-size: 13px; } .dim { color: var(--fg-dim); font-size: 12px; margin-top: 6px; }\n  #none { display: none; color: var(--fg-dim); margin-top: 14px; } @media (max-width: 560px) { .r { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 2px; } }\n</style>\n<h3>${esc(sheet.title)} cheat sheet</h3>\n<input id=\"q\" placeholder=\"Search this sheet\" autofocus>\n<div class=\"dim\">Click a row to put its code at the cursor of your file.</div>\n<div id=\"all\">${body}</div><div id=\"none\">Nothing matches.</div>\n<script>\n  const q = document.getElementById('q'), none = document.getElementById('none');\n  q.addEventListener('input', () => {\n    const s = q.value.trim().toLowerCase(); let n = 0;\n    document.querySelectorAll('.r').forEach((r) => { const ok = !s || r.dataset.q.includes(s); r.style.display = ok ? '' : 'none'; if (ok) n++; });\n    document.querySelectorAll('h4').forEach((h) => { let x = h.nextElementSibling, any = false; while (x && x.classList.contains('r')) { if (x.style.display !== 'none') any = true; x = x.nextElementSibling; } h.style.display = any ? '' : 'none'; });\n    none.style.display = n ? 'none' : 'block';\n  });\n  document.getElementById('all').addEventListener('click', (e) => { const r = e.target.closest('.r'); if (r) ferrumPanel.postMessage({ type: 'insert', code: r.dataset.c }); });\n</script>`;\n}\n\nexports._test = { SHEETS, rows, filter, page };\n\nexports.activate = function (context) {\n  const open = {};\n  async function show(key) {\n    const html = page(key);\n    if (open[key]) { open[key].setHtml(html); return; }\n    const p = await ferrum.window.showPanel({ title: SHEETS[key].title + ' cheat sheet', html });\n    open[key] = p;\n    p.onDidClose(() => delete open[key]);\n    p.onMessage(async (m) => {\n      if (m.type !== 'insert') return;\n      const doc = await ferrum.editor.active();\n      if (!doc) return ferrum.window.showMessage('Open a file to insert into.', 'warn');\n      await ferrum.editor.insert(String(m.code || '').slice(0, 2000));\n    });\n  }\n  for (const key of Object.keys(SHEETS)) context.subscriptions.push(ferrum.commands.register('cheatSheets.' + key, () => show(key)));\n  context.subscriptions.push(\n    ferrum.commands.register('cheatSheets.search', async () => {\n      const q = await ferrum.window.showInputBox({ prompt: 'Search every cheat sheet', placeholder: 'undo, center, 404, flex, replace...' });\n      if (!q) return;\n      const hits = Object.keys(SHEETS).flatMap((k) => filter(k, q).map((r) => ({ ...r, sheet: SHEETS[k].title })));\n      if (!hits.length) return ferrum.window.showMessage('Nothing found for \"' + q + '\".');\n      const pick = await ferrum.window.showQuickPick(hits.slice(0, 80).map((r) => ({ label: r.code.split('\\n')[0], detail: r.note, description: r.sheet + ' · ' + r.group, code: r.code })), { placeholder: hits.length + ' results. Pick one to insert it.' });\n      if (pick) await ferrum.editor.insert(pick.code);\n    }),\n    ferrum.commands.register('cheatSheets.pick', async () => {\n      const pick = await ferrum.window.showQuickPick(Object.entries(SHEETS).map(([k, s]) => ({ label: s.title, detail: Object.values(s.groups).reduce((n, l) => n + l.length, 0) + ' entries', key: k })), { placeholder: 'Open a cheat sheet' });\n      if (pick) await show(pick.key);\n    }),\n  );\n};\n\nexports.deactivate = function () {};\n"},"README.md":{"encoding":"utf8","content":"# Cheat Sheets\n\nSeven reference sheets, each in a panel with a search box. **Click a row to put its code in your file** at the cursor.\n\n| Sheet | What is in it |\n| --- | --- |\n| **Git** | Start, save work, branches, remotes, history, undo, stash, tags |\n| **Regular expressions** | Characters, anchors, quantifiers, groups, lookarounds, flags, replacements, common patterns |\n| **Vim** | Modes, movement, editing, search and replace, files, macros and marks |\n| **Markdown** | Text, lists, links, images, code, tables, footnotes, collapsible sections |\n| **HTTP status codes** | 1xx to 5xx with a plain explanation |\n| **CSS Flexbox** | Container and item properties and common recipes |\n| **CSS Grid** | Container and item properties and common recipes |\n\n**Search All Cheat Sheets...** looks in all of them at once (\"undo\", \"center\", \"404\", \"replace\") and inserts the pick.\n\nThe sheets are built into the extension, so they work offline. No permissions needed.\n"}}}